      ],
      "observed": "R8 is listed with value \"2.2\" in the netlist and is modeled as 2.2 Ω in the SPICE deck, connected from +3V3 to the MAX3485 B line (Net-(U1-B)).",
      "expected": "The specification requires R8 to be 2.2 kΩ as part of the MAX3485 A/B bias/fail-safe network. R15 uses the same LCSC part C4190 and is explicitly 2.2k, supporting that R8 should also be 2.2 kΩ.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R8\")\n      (value \"2.2\")\n      ...\n      (field (name \"LCSC\") \"C4190\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n(node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R8 +3V3 Net-_U1-B_ 2.2"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "| R6, R7, R8, R15 | 2k, 20k, 2.2k, 2.2k | Bias/pull network on the MAX3485 A/B differential lines and DE/RE enable line. |"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R15\")\n      (value \"2.2k\")\n      ...\n      (field (name \"LCSC\") \"C4190\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If R8 is populated as 2.2 Ω, the MAX3485 B line is pulled almost to +3V3 instead of being properly biased with the intended 2.2 kΩ network. In serial mode this can destroy the intended fail-safe/idle differential state and may cause driver contention or degraded communication when the transceiver pulls B low; it may also draw excessive current through the driver output.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design otherwise matches the specification, but R8 is recorded and simulated as 2.2 Ω instead of the specified 2.2 kΩ, which is a plausible value/BOM anomaly affecting the MAX3485 RS-485 bias network."
}

